R completes required patching required by NGC IT Security.<br></span><!--StartFragment--><span data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">Both collector up and Running</span><!--EndFragment--><span style=\"font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 16px;\"></span>','By Customer',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1h 38m',98,'2026-09-17 15:22:33','2026-09-17 16:48:36'),(760,'INC-321',NULL,'Azure: Activated Severity: 0 MTH No Historian Read','Dear Team,<br><br>We would like to inform you about a recent occurrence of a \'No Historian Read\' alert at MTH.<br>Our team has conducted an investigation and prepared a detailed report to provide you with all the necessary information.<br><br>Please find the following details:<br><br>- Plant Name: MTH[MTH-APPSVR]<br>- \'No Historian Read\' Alert Details: [NGCXPILAVM1]<br><br>- Duration: 40 minutes plant MTH is down.<br>- Impact: Data is not flowing into FactoryEye for MTH while this alert is active.<br><br><br>- Steps Taken:<br><br>We have identified that we were not reading data from the Historian server and are not able to ping.<br>We have identified that we cannot read data from the Historian server. We ask that someone on the NGC technical support team check the server’s network access, power to the server and/or the plant, the Historian licensing is active and lastly restart the server if all else fails.<br>Please inform us when you have a resolution to the issue, and/or you have verified that the server is operational.<br>We understand the importance of resolving this matter promptly, and we appreciate your collaboration towards ensuring a swift resolution.<br><br>Thank you for your attention to this matter.','critical','closed',20,'Vibha Khanke',20,'NGC',3,'Historian',NULL,'Historian',8,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',NULL,'2026-09-18 06:22','2026-09-18 06:22:00','2026-09-18 06:22:00.000000','2026-09-18 13:21','2026-09-18 13:21:00','2026-09-18 13:21:00.000000','2026-09-18','GMT','Etc/UTC',6,59,419,'6h 59m','MTH Plant was down due to unplanned outage','The historian service start processing data.&nbsp;','By Stakeholder',NULL,NULL,'5m',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'6h 59m',419,'2026-09-18 07:14:49','2026-09-18 13:34:21'),(761,'INC-322',NULL,'Coralogix Alert on magic / Toridoll- Average K8s Node Memory Utilization Higher than 80%','We\'ve detected that the query has exceeded 80 for over 100% of the following','critical','closed',18,'Shantanu Patil',18,'TORIDOLL',20,'TORIDOLL',NULL,'Infrastructure',1,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',NULL,'2026-09-18 23:25','2026-09-18 23:25:00','2026-09-18 14:25:00.000000','2026-09-19 00:51','2026-09-19 00:51:00','2026-09-18 15:51:00.000000','2026-09-19','JST','Asia/Tokyo',0,0,0,NULL,'High memory consumption.','Auto-resolved after some time.','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'5m',5,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1h 26m',86,'2026-09-18 14:41:03','2026-09-23 07:08:46'),(763,'INC-323',NULL,'Coralogix Alert on magic / Christie Digital_EC2 Low Free Disk Space','<div>Hi Team,</div><div><br></div><div>We have received an alert for free disk space low on Christie Digital Production EC2 environment.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Observations:</b></div><div>There is low disk space for the C: Drive on Christie Digital Production EC2 environment. When investigated we observed that xpi logs were consuming 18.9 GB of disk space from following directory - C:\\xpi\\xpi4141\\Runtime\\Logs\\java</div><div><br></div><div><b>Actions:</b></div><div>We cleared logs from the following directory C:\\xpi\\xpi4141\\Runtime\\Logs\\java</div><div>The current free space is 28.6 GB. The issue has been resolved.</div>','critical','closed',16,'Pooja Thakkhi',16,'Christie Digital',12,NULL,NULL,'Infrastructure',1,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',NULL,'2026-09-21 19:39','2026-09-21 19:39:00','2026-09-21 14:09:00.000000','2026-09-21 20:26','2026-09-21 20:26:00','2026-09-21 14:56:00.000000','2026-09-21','IST','Asia/Kolkata',0,0,0,NULL,'Free disk space low on Christie Digital Production EC2 environment.&nbsp;','We cleared logs from the following directory C:\\xpi\\xpi4141\\Runtime\\Logs\\javaThe current free space is 28.6 GB. The issue has been resolved.','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'2m',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'47m',47,'2026-09-21 18:23:14','2026-09-22 06:35:35'),(764,'INC-324',NULL,'Production project - JDE_emailforms errors for project Christie Digital.','<div>Hi Team,</div><div><br></div><div>As part of our investigation, we found that the project build had failed, which caused the reported issue.</div><div>We have successfully rebuilt the project and deployed the updated version to the environment. Please verify from your side and confirm whether the JDE_emailforms&nbsp; project is now working as expected.</div><div><br></div><div>We will continue to monitor the environment and assist further if required.</div>','critical','closed',16,'Pooja Thakkhi',16,'Christie Digital',12,NULL,NULL,'Integration',17,'Integration',NULL,NULL,'[]',NULL,'2026-09-21 11:17','2026-09-21 11:17:00','2026-09-21 15:17:00.000000','2026-09-21 11:52','2026-09-21 11:52:00','2026-09-21 15:52:00.000000','2026-09-21','EST','America/New_York',0,0,0,NULL,'JDE_emailforms errors for project Christie Digital','We have successfully rebuilt the project and deployed the updated version to the environment.The issue is resolved and confirmed by customer.','By OC Team',NULL,NULL,'2m',2,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'35m',35,'2026-09-21 18:34:47','2026-09-22 06:04:22'),(765,'INC-325',NULL,'Production project - INOWAP_Lookups for project Christie Digital.','<div>Hi Team,</div><div><br></div><div>As part of our investigation, we found that the project build had failed, which caused the reported issue.</div><div>We have successfully rebuilt the project and deployed the updated version to the environment. Please verify from your side and confirm whether the&nbsp; INOWAP_Lookups project is now working as expected.</div><div><br></div><div>We w